  "rules": "A group \"moves\" in a frame when its world matrix changed since the last audited frame (by more than 1e-6). Groups that moved by the same rigid motion (a MiR with its cabinet, its holders and the parts on them) form one cluster and are not checked against each other: their relative poses didn't change, so no new contact can appear between them. Every visible body of a moving group is checked against every other visible body except its own group's subtree and ancestors, the arms and what they hold (the arm checks do those), liquids, and the floor with its markings (anything whose top is within FLOOR_MM, 6 mm, of z = 0: tape is paint, and a MiR's skirt is drawn down to the floor): world boxes first, all at once, then FCL on the meshes of the pairs whose boxes overlap (BVHs built only for those). The contacts a group had at its last pose before it started moving are its baseline and are left out while it keeps moving, until that pair comes apart; a new contact counts if depth() puts it deeper than DEPTH_MM (1.5 mm), so a tray set down on a table or a MiR rolling onto a floor plate isn't reported."
